417 true] [17592186425086 1071 "The discrete random variable $X\\in Z$ can be approximated by the continuous random variable $Y.$ By applying an appropriate continuity correction, $P(X=5)$ can be approximated as" 13194139534545 17592186045417 true] [17592186425086 1072 #uuid "6a72d914-d1dc-54af-a5be-bb57f769ce56" 13194139534545 17592186045417 true] [17592186425086 1074 "We construct an interval around $X=5$ with a radius of $0.5:$\n\n![](images/b8/b87c1f5bb39d9bd7fe5a46695eb8428909fc40c0e489fd12b054bbd77be8127f.png)\n\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=5) & ≈P(5-0.5\\le Y\\le 5+0.5) \\\\  & =P(4.5\\le Y\\le 5.5).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534545 17592186045417 true] [17592186425087 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425083 13194139534545 17592186045417 true] [17592186425087 1069 "q-132234" 13194139534545 17592186045417 true] [17592186425087 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534545 17592186045417 true] [17592186425087 1071 "The discrete random variable $X\\in Z$ can be approximated by the continuous random variable $Y.$ By applying an appropriate continuity correction, $P(X<17)$ can be approximated as" 13194139534545 17592186045417 true] [17592186425087 1072 #uuid "72c5955a-7dbc-59eb-bd3a-0c79c37d7f53" 13194139534545 17592186045417 true] [17592186425087 1074 "To apply the appropriate continuity correction, we first rewrite the strict inequality as follows:\n\n$$\nP(X<17)=P(X\\le 16)\n$$\n\nThen, we extend the endpoint of the interval $X\\le 16$ by $0.5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 16) & ≈P(Y\\le 16+0.5) \\\\  & =P(Y\\le 16.5)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534545 17592186045417 true] [17592186425088 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425085 13194139534545 17592186045417 true] [17592186425088 1069 "q-132237" 13194139534545 17592186045417 true] [17592186425088 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534545 17592186045417 true] [17592186425088 1071 "The discrete random variable $X\\in Z$ can be approximated by the continuous random variable $Y.$ By applying an appropriate continuity correction, $P(X>8)$ can be approximated as" 13194139534545 17592186045417 true] [17592186425088 1072 #uuid "baf96d37-475c-5239-92e4-1c5876314e32" 13194139534545 17592186045417 true] [17592186425088 1074 "To apply the appropriate continuity correction, we first rewrite the strict inequality as follows:\n\n$$\nP(X>8)=P(X\\ge 9)\n$$\n\nThen, we extend the endpoint of the interval $X\\ge 9$ by $0.5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 9) & ≈P(Y\\ge 9-0.5) \\\\  & =P(Y\\ge 8.5)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534545 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-01d60f05-c149-5def-b6ca-6ac37c02ecce" 17592186425063 "answer-07428db6-e061-5594-af12-24a5080b1157" 17592186425064 "answer-07e95014-9cde-5766-9827-921ed2bfc5e7" 17592186425065 "answer-200fbb3c-40ed-5f05-be1e-0229439b9ea6" 17592186425066 "answer-2f661294-8d1d-5989-ab1b-c340c60acbc3" 17592186425067 "answer-3564fafa-635b-5b67-920a-8b89ad998edd" 17592186425068 "answer-36c79b55-d3d7-513c-bea5-e6b4e2f37fb2" 17592186425069 "answer-5624fc6b-71f5-5237-8bc4-a22cff8b950b" 17592186425070 "answer-5a62bd9c-6c24-515e-9f78-c2ed702816a1" 17592186425071 "answer-6c01b248-edc0-5c3a-afe7-84054dabefc2" 17592186425072 "answer-80edd3e9-db44-5510-afad-060f1e61caba" 17592186425073 "answer-8f67a7a7-0a33-55ce-bae5-e1103dafd6ee" 17592186425074 "answer-aea03d54-47ff-5704-91a4-d89cf538b880" 17592186425075 "answer-b4a26668-5f4b-5cc5-bd3b-0f6627b55524" 17592186425076 "answer-b729172a-2775-5903-9a85-cf462a6f041e" 17592186425077 "answer-b8439328-6909-5b99-807f-3c207a09c9ff" 17592186425078 "answer-c7e6822b-04c7-5aa7-af4d-8a07b0a0c783" 17592186425079 "answer-d18d5c57-96a7-5b82-aa6b-d7f2b64a211a" 17592186425080 "answer-e302ee78-c6a0-50a1-a03c-b11c2116add8" 17592186425081 "answer-ed9cf813-6d76-5f99-881d-b8d9cc313502" 17592186425082 "answer-field-80373b3a-df08-56fd-91af-f3a698f5efbb" 17592186425083 "answer-field-8989c1e9-ef6a-5ef2-be82-e950e4719a8d" 17592186425084 "answer-field-8a65ee43-9417-5b75-9427-c7a5605ab37b" 17592186425085 "question-6a72d914-d1dc-54af-a5be-bb57f76